### Note on Meeko (LGPL-2.1) — corrected against the delivery brief
The brief for this package said "Meeko/BSD-3". **Meeko 0.8.0 declares LGPL-2.1**
(`meeko-0.8.0.dist-info/METADATA`, `License: LGPL-2.1`). Consequences:

* Meeko is used as an **unmodified installed dependency**, imported by Python at
  runtime — the usual "use a library, don't relicense it" case. No Meeko source is
  copied into this package, so this package's MIT license is unaffected.
* If you redistribute a **modified** Meeko, LGPL-2.1 obligations apply to that
  modified library (source availability, relinking).
* If your organisation forbids LGPL dependencies, the ligand/receptor preparation
  step cannot be reproduced with this package as-is; `mk_prepare_*` is the only
  path here that turns RDKit molecules into AutoDock PDBQT.

